GFOpenTorrent: one copy at a time through an ARexx port, no tray, and
free space through Info().
AmigaOS has no named mutex, DDE, tray icon or taskbar button: application
asks the first copy's port (GFOPENTORRENT.1, compat/gfot_rexx.cpp) in
place of wxSingleInstanceChecker and wxClient; ipc/server.hpp declares the
ARexx server (compat/picotorrent/ipc_server_amiga.cpp); the tray icon and
taskbar button are nothing (compat/gfot_notray.hpp); Configuration reads
the tray settings as false (compat/gfot_settings.cpp); libpico.h has no
dllexport; MainFrame asks the save volume's free space through
compat/gfot_disk.cpp in place of GetDiskFreeSpaceEx and sets no window
icon (Workbench windows have none; the icon is the .info file) and,
after Preferences, restarts through wxStandardPaths; a .torrent file
opens by its toolkit file name (libstdc++ takes no wstring). Each
change sits under __WXOPENLAYOUT__, Windows' code as it was.
